Mills 8A
Copyright 2026 heiner

Fonts
-----

The font files (*.otf, *.pfb, *.tfm, *.vf, *.enc, mills8a.map) contain
glyphs from Latin Modern and Latin Modern Math, copyright B. Jackowski,
J. M. Nowacki, P. Strzelczyk and P. Pianowski (on behalf of TeX users
groups), released under the GUST Font License. They are a modified version
of Latin Modern and are distributed under the same licence: see
GUST-FONT-LICENSE.txt (the LaTeX Project Public License 1.3c or later).
The unmodified fonts: https://ctan.org/pkg/lm and https://ctan.org/pkg/lm-math

Changes to Latin Modern:
- Mills8A-Math: Latin Modern Math with its letters, Greek, figures,
  operators, \cdot and \cdots, display sum, product and integral and their
  script variants replaced by glyphs traced from 1940s printing in Monotype
  Modern 8A; script sizes and shifts in the MATH table changed; the other
  glyphs and the MATH table are Latin Modern Math's.
- The text fonts: glyphs traced from the same printing; the accents other
  than the dieresis and the symbols the printing lacks (# % @ \ ^ _ { } ~
  § † ‡ ¶ « » ß Æ Œ Ø Ł and others) are Latin Modern Roman's, thickened
  and repositioned; bold, bold italic and 9 pt versions of these are
  further thickened or scaled.
- Unicode supplements: missing European letters and currency signs are
  taken from Latin Modern and scaled to Mills 8A's heights; combining marks
  and their positioning tables are added using the existing accents.
- The pdfTeX fonts (*.pfb, *.tfm, *.vf, *.enc) are conversions of the
  above, split into TeX's 256-glyph encodings.
- All are renamed (Mills 8A, m8a*).

